<speak>Mostly the latter. The inbox is not the problem. I have been treating all incoming correspondence as equally urgent, and that makes it harder to read anything properly. When I travel, I sometimes sit down intending to read a personal document and end up answering a question about packaging because it appears at the top of the phone. Then the personal document remains unread. I would like bank correspondence to be easy to locate when I am ready to give it attention, rather than make it compete with everything else.</speak>